# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Wild Titan), edited. The Wild Titan: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_titan_arrived
Narrator: A cluster of mining huts on a snowy ridge, the shafts boarded up, and cracks running through the frozen ground.
check Dexterity DC 18 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You hear the rumble in time and press against the rock face as the stones fall past.
set mf_titan_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A rockfall catches a hero on the slope and leaves them bruised and shaken.
damage 4d8 bludgeoning party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You climb the slope, and the whole mountain rumbles, dropping stones the size of cartwheels.
time +60
check Dexterity DC 18 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_jory_miner [sad]: He says his wife and boy went up to the pass for firewood and did not come down, and the mountain has been roaring for days.
set mf_titan_asked
quest mf_titan asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_jory_miner [weary]: He says the rocks fell on another hamlet last night and asks if you can help.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_titan_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_jory_miner [angry]: Rocks come down a mile at a time, fire will not burn near the peaks, and the roars rise until strong men run mad with them.
-> menu

~ where
mf_jory_miner [sad]: He says the mountain itself woke, a thing made of the wild and forgotten by whoever made it, and it walks the high passes.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_jory_miner [neutral]: He says the old rune stones on the slopes may tell of its maker; somebody who reads runes might learn how to hurt it.
* [History DC 18] Read the old rune stones on the slope -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Nature DC 18] Compare the runes against the mountain's lore -> a_ok | a_slow
* Copy every rune on the slope by hand -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_jory_miner [smile]: The stones tell of a maker and a binding, and somewhere among them a name that is half erased.
time +60
set mf_titan_found
set mf_titan_clue_a
quest mf_titan trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You spend hours on the freezing slope copying runes with numb fingers, and the story of the Titan comes together out of them.
time +300
set mf_titan_found
quest mf_titan trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_grizzle_hunter [neutral]: He tells you to keep your voice down, and that he has been trailing the thing for three days and it is bigger than the book of stories says.
set mf_titan_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_grizzle_hunter [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_titan_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_titan_found and not flag.mf_titan_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_grizzle_hunter [neutral]: He says it follows the high ridges and goes to the summit plateau to roar, and anyone who hears it too long goes berserk.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_grizzle_hunter [neutral]: He says he can show you its trail, if you can keep up and keep quiet.
* [Survival DC 18] Track the Titan along the ridges -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Animal Handling DC 18] Follow the animals fleeing its path -> b_ok | b_slow
* Climb the ridge slowly and follow the cracked earth -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_grizzle_hunter [smile]: The trail is clear once you see it, boulders thrown aside, and it leads to the summit plateau.
time +60
set mf_titan_found
set mf_titan_clue_b
quest mf_titan trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: You lose hours on the false trails, but the cracked earth leads you to the summit at last.
time +300
set mf_titan_found
quest mf_titan trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_grizzle_hunter [neutral]: He says the maker's name is carved as a glyph on a big stone down the slope; carve it large enough and the Titan sickens by it.
* [History DC 18] Transcribe the maker's glyph from the stones -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Athletics DC 18] Work out the glyph's meaning and carve it true -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Carve the glyph out clumsily, over and over, until it holds -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_grizzle_hunter [smile]: You carve the glyph deep into a great flat stone, and the air around it goes cold and strange.
time +60
give mf_glyph_stone
set mf_titan_weak
quest mf_titan ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: Your first dozen carvings are worthless, but through the night a good one emerges, big and square and true.
time +300
give mf_glyph_stone
set mf_titan_weak
quest mf_titan ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The summit plateau opens above, ringed with broken stones, and the ground trembles with slow footfalls.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_titan_reveals
Narrator: The Wild Titan rises over the summit, a giant of rock and root and ice, its fists the size of cottages.
cutscene mf_titan_reveals_2
Narrator: It roars, and the whole mountain answers.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_titan_weak
combat mf_titan_weak
elif level >= 16
combat mf_titan_full
else
combat mf_titan_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_titan_falls
Narrator: The Titan staggers, its great arms hanging, and slowly sits down on the summit like a mountain settling.
cutscene mf_titan_falls_2
Narrator: Below, the moon turns its face south and east, toward the place the dead are buried.
cutscene end
set mf_titan_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give runestone_of_the_wild_titan
quest mf_titan slain
xp milestone
Narrator: At Maidenmist the graves are already opening, one after another, like mouths.
-> END
